                    },
                    "message": "Why?  These conditions in the past have been pretty trivial to find through code inspection?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "When you are looking at the journal later, how do you narrow down which of the 100+ schemas we support is causing it?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Aopenbmc%2Fbmcweb%20no_content&type=code\n\nThere's only 10 places we call that in handler code.  (FWIW, I thought it was 5)"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "I don't know if this is needed long term but we have seen these traces in the journal. Ideally, these are just fixed (Abiola is going to work on that). I don't care that much if this is accepted. It could be ran with in a build to find the places this is logging from. I would say this commit does make the trace more valuable but i don't care that much"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Sorry, I should've been more clear with that.  This patch is fine, but long term we should clean this up."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
